## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10 · Integration test class (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 4: Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Affected:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← No assertion — passes even if every insert silently fails
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence. If `Insert` swallows exceptions or silently no-ops, this test still passes.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 1: Conditional Test Logic

**Affected:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Risk:** One branch never executes (since the test inserts a plain `User`, the `PremiumUser` branch is dead code). The test appears to cover both paths but only exercises one — a hidden coverage gap.

**Fix:** Split into two focused tests or assert the expected concrete type:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<User>(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 3: Sleepy Test

**Affected:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);  // ← Hard 3-second wall-clock wait

Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk:** Adds 3 seconds to every test run. On slower CI agents the 3 s may not be enough (flake); on fast machines it's wasted time. Non-deterministic either way.

**Integration calibration note:** Even for integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` remains a smell (per Camara et al. 2021, it correlates with flakiness). Severity stays High.

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout or use an async wait primitive:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Affected:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// ← 4 assertions, zero message parameters
```

**Risk:** When one of these fails in CI, the failure output is `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>.` — no context on *which property* or *why* it matters. Diagnosis requires reading source.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-designed and exhibit no smells:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Minimal, verifies absence correctly |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion (3) is self-documenting given 3 inserts |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good async pattern, clear assertion |

The use of in-memory SQLite (`Data Source=:memory:`) as a hermetic substitute avoids **Mystery Guest** — well done.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add count/content assertion to `BulkInsert` | 2 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Remove `if` branch, assert expected type directly | 5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll/retry helper | 15 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to multi-assert tests | 5 min |

Fixes 1–2 prevent **false passes** (tests that can never fail). Fix 3 prevents **flakiness**. Fix 4 improves **debuggability**.
